# M-Pesa Daraja API Configuration
# Copy this file to your Supabase project secrets configuration
# DO NOT commit actual credentials to version control

# M-Pesa API Credentials
# Obtain these from: https://developer.safaricom.co.ke/
MPESA_CONSUMER_KEY=your_consumer_key_here
MPESA_CONSUMER_SECRET=your_consumer_secret_here

# M-Pesa Business Configuration
MPESA_SHORTCODE=174379
MPESA_PASSKEY=your_passkey_here

# Environment Mode
# Options: 'sandbox' or 'production'
# Default: 'sandbox'
MPESA_ENVIRONMENT=sandbox

# Callback URLs (configured in Supabase Edge Functions)
MPESA_CALLBACK_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co/functions/v1/mpesa-callback
MPESA_TIMEOUT_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co/functions/v1/mpesa-timeout

# Safaricom IP Whitelist (comma-separated)
# These IPs are allowed to send callbacks to your system
SAFARICOM_IP_WHITELIST=196.201.214.200,196.201.214.206,196.201.213.114,196.201.214.207,196.201.214.208,196.201.213.44,196.201.212.127,196.201.212.128,196.201.212.129,196.201.212.136

## Configuration Instructions

### 1. Sandbox Setup (Development/Testing)

1. Go to https://developer.safaricom.co.ke/
2. Create an account and login
3. Create a new app
4. Select "Lipa Na M-Pesa Online" product
5. Copy your Consumer Key and Consumer Secret
6. Use sandbox shortcode: 174379
7. Get test passkey from sandbox documentation

### 2. Production Setup

1. Complete Safaricom's production application process
2. Obtain production credentials
3. Use your assigned business shortcode
4. Get production passkey from Safaricom
5. Set MPESA_ENVIRONMENT=production

### 3. Setting Variables in Supabase

Using Supabase CLI:
```bash
supabase secrets set MPESA_CONSUMER_KEY=your_key_here
supabase secrets set MPESA_CONSUMER_SECRET=your_secret_here
supabase secrets set MPESA_SHORTCODE=174379
supabase secrets set MPESA_PASSKEY=your_passkey_here
supabase secrets set MPESA_ENVIRONMENT=sandbox
supabase secrets set MPESA_CALLBACK_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co/functions/v1/mpesa-callback
```

Using Supabase Dashboard:
1. Go to Project Settings > Edge Functions
2. Navigate to Secrets section
3. Add each variable with its value
4. Save changes

### 4. Verifying Configuration

Run credential validation:
```typescript
import { validateCredentials } from "./shared/mpesa-auth.ts";

try {
  validateCredentials();
  console.log("✅ Configuration valid!");
} catch (error) {
  console.error("❌ Configuration error:", error.message);
}
```

## Security Notes

⚠️ **NEVER commit actual credentials to version control**
⚠️ **Keep sandbox and production credentials separate**
⚠️ **Rotate credentials regularly (quarterly recommended)**
⚠️ **Monitor for unauthorized access attempts**

## Testing Credentials

For sandbox testing, use Safaricom's test phone numbers:
- Test number: 254708374149 (auto-completes payment)
- Test number: 254708374150 (auto-cancels payment)

Sandbox transactions are free and don't use real money.

## Support

For credential issues:
- Sandbox: Check Safaricom Developer Portal
- Production: Contact Safaricom Business Support

For implementation issues:
- Review logs in Supabase Dashboard > Edge Functions > Logs
- Check mpesa-auth module documentation
- Verify all environment variables are set correctly
